project:
  name: BookBot - RAG-Based PDF QA System
  description: >
    Build a full-stack AI web application that allows users to upload PDF books, organize them into libraries, and ask questions based on their content using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). The app should provide accurate responses from uploaded documents and maintain chat history.

  goals:
    - Enable users to upload and manage PDFs under multiple libraries.
    - Parse and embed PDF content for semantic search and RAG.
    - Build a chat interface to ask context-aware questions using LLMs.
    - Maintain and resume chat history per user and per library.
    - Ensure UI is modern, responsive, and user-friendly.

  stack:
    frontend:
      framework: React
      styling: TailwindCSS
      pages:
        - Library List (create/switch libraries)
        - Upload View (with drag-and-drop & progress bar)
        - Chat Interface (chat window + source context)
        - History View (view and resume past sessions)
    backend:
      framework: FastAPI
      endpoints:
        - POST /upload: Handle PDF parsing, chunking, and embedding
        - POST /chat: Handle question, retrieve relevant context, generate answer
        - GET /libraries: List user libraries
        - GET /history: List past conversations
      libraries:
        - PyMuPDF (PDF parsing)
        - LangChain or custom RAG pipeline
        - ChromaDB (Vector Store)
        - SentenceTransformers (Embedding)
        - SQLite or PostgreSQL (for chat history)

  requirements:
    - Chunk PDFs (e.g., 500 tokens, 100 overlap) for embedding.
    - Use vector DB (ChromaDB or FAISS) for retrieval.
    - Embed content using `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` or OpenAI embeddings.
    - Use OpenAI GPT-3.5/GPT-4 for chat responses.
    - Reject out-of-scope questions gracefully (with fallback message).
    - Store chat history with timestamps, user ID, and library context.

  constraints:
    - Clean modular code, clear folder structure.
    - Use `.env` for keys and secrets.
    - Containerize backend with Docker.
    - Use async FastAPI where possible.
    - Protect user data and ensure proper API rate handling.

  extensions:
    - Optional: JWT/Firebase user login
    - Optional: PDF preview
    - Optional: Tagging PDFs or keyword search within library
    - Optional: Export chat to PDF

  tips:
    - Start with backend structure, setup FastAPI app and vector store.
    - Build embedding + upload logic before frontend.
    - Use LangChain's `RetrievalQA` if using LangChain; otherwise use custom chain.
    - Use React Router for page navigation.
    - Keep conversation context per session or allow resuming via history tab.

  references:
    - LangChain docs: https://docs.langchain.com
    - ChromaDB: https://www.trychroma.com
    - SentenceTransformers: https://www.sbert.net
    - PyMuPDF: https://pymupdf.readthedocs.io


